          "type": "turn",
          "question": "If someone has a raised blood pressure reading but no diagnosis of hypertension, which chapter does that belong in?",
          "answer": "According to ICD-10 classification systems, a raised blood pressure reading in someone who has not been diagnosed with hypertension belongs in Chapter 18, which covers \"symptoms, signs and abnormal findings\" (R00-R99). This is because it is considered a finding rather than a disease until a formal diagnosis of hypertension is made. The codes R00 to R09 are relevant for symptoms and signs involving the circulatory system, including an elevated blood pressure reading without a hypertension diagnosis. (Sources: `coding-hypertension-i10`, `coding-icd10-chapter-18-symptoms`)\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
